        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "73935e80-1bd3-522f-807a-6e38d1f8b38f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tessa Nuku, Brendon Boney\n- Organizations: Microwave Jenny, Central Coast Council\n- Places: Wagga Wagga, Ulladulla, Umina Beach, New South Wales, Australia\n- Topics: Indigenous backgrounds, music, film\n\nFacts:\n- Microwave Jenny is an Australian pop, folk, and jazz duet consisting of Tessa Nuku on vocals and Brendon Boney on guitar and vocals.\n- Tessa Nuku and Brendon Boney both have Indigenous backgrounds.\n- Brendon Boney was born and raised in Wagga Wagga, Australia.\n- Tessa Nuku was born in Ulladulla, New South Wales, and later grew up in Umina Beach, New South Wales.\n- Brendon Boney was the singing voice for the character Willie in the film Bran Nue Dae.\n- Umina Beach is a suburb on the Central Coast of New South Wales, Australia, within the Central Coast Council local government area.",
